hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1695","###\n Narrated to us by Bashr bin Mu'adh, he said: Narrated to us by Bashr, meaning Ibn al-Mufaddal, he said: Narrated to us by Abd al-Rahman, who is Ibn Ishaq, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl bin Sa'd (RA), who said: \During the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," women were instructed in prayer not to raise their heads until the men had taken their seats"," due to the tightness of their garments"," lest the women see the"""
